From: Joonwon Kang <joonwonkang@google.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Nov 2025 06:22:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mailbox: Prevent out-of-bounds access in
 fw_mbox_index_xlate()
Git-commit: fcd7f96c783626c07ee3ed75fa3739a8a2052310
Patch-mainline: v7.0-rc1
References: CVE-2026-43281 bsc#1264534

[ Use ->args_count, equivalent, reference: ba879dfc057487 ("mailbox: Allow
  controller specific mapping using fwnode") ]

Although it is guided that `#mbox-cells` must be at least 1, there are
many instances of `#mbox-cells = <0>;` in the device tree. If that is
the case and the corresponding mailbox controller does not provide
`fw_xlate` and of_xlate` function pointers, `fw_mbox_index_xlate()` will
be used by default and out-of-bounds accesses could occur due to lack of
bounds check in that function.

Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Signed-off-by: Joonwon Kang <joonwonkang@google.com>
Signed-off-by: Jassi Brar <jassisinghbrar@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: David Sterba <dsterba@suse.com>
---
 drivers/mailbox/mailbox.c |    6 ++----
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/mailbox/mailbox.c
+++ b/drivers/mailbox/mailbox.c
@@ -499,12 +499,10 @@ static struct mbox_chan *
 of_mbox_index_xlate(struct mbox_controller *mbox,
 		    const struct of_phandle_args *sp)
 {
-	int ind = sp->args[0];
-
-	if (ind >= mbox->num_chans)
+	if (sp->args_count < 1 || sp->args[0] >= mbox->num_chans)
 		return ERR_PTR(-EINVAL);
 
-	return &mbox->chans[ind];
+	return &mbox->chans[sp->args[0]];
 }
 
